  "label": "User projected onto the textual question",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'mommy, why am i getting christmas presents in august?' because the text uses the first-person pronoun 'i', which directly addresses the viewer as if they are the child asking the question. This creates an immediate identification with the child's perspective, making the user feel as though they are the one experiencing the confusion and distress depicted in the image.",
